      "courseId": "crs-cmsc131",
      "title": "Discussion 1: Client-Side vs Server-Side Rendering (SSR) in Modern SPAs",
      "prompt": "Evaluate the trade-offs between Client-Side Rendering (CSR), Server-Side Rendering (SSR), and Static Site Generation (SSG). Which architecture would you recommend for an institutional LMS like GABAY that integrates with Likha ERP and requires real-time offline sync? Justify your choice with at least two architectural considerations (TTFB, caching, SEO, or security).",
      "authorId": "usr-fac-1",
      "authorName": "Faculty 1",
      "authorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507003211169-0a1dd7228f2d?w=150&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
      "authorRole": "faculty",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-03T10:00:00Z",
      "isGraded": true,
      "pointsPossible": 25,
      "dueDate": "2026-09-18T23:59:00Z",
      "pinned": true,
      "locked": false,
      "usersMustPostBeforeReplies": true,
      "groupAssignment": "All Students",
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "drep-1",
          "discussionId": "disc-131-1",
          "authorId": "usr-stud-1",
          "authorName": "Student 1",
          "authorAvatar": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1500648767791-00dcc994a43e?w=150&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80",
          "authorRole": "student",
          "content": "For GABAY LMS, a hybrid approach (SSR with client-side hydration) offers the best balance. Initial page loads benefit from pre-rendered shells with zero blank screen time, while authenticated state synchronization with Likha ERP can operate over client-side WebSocket/REST workers with local indexedDB offline caching.",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-04T15:30:00Z",
          "likes": 4,
          "likedBy": ["usr-fac-1"]
        },
        {
